in just a few weeks now thousands of  ccsd students will be back in the  classroom for the first time in nearly a  year  campuses will reopen in phases on march  1st  starting with pre-k through third grade  bianca holman is live in our newsroom  with more on the district's plan hi  bianca  afternoon alex the district has  developed this 235 page document  and it's outlining the reopening plan to  protect students and adult  it shares cleaning of the cleaning  protocols and what students can expect  when they return  now the young students will start on a  hybrid model of learning  including face-to-face instruction on  march 1st  all students and staff must wear face  coverings with a few exceptions  custodians will have enhanced enhanced  cleaning protocols  plus updated hvac technologies are in  the works to improve  indoor air quality now for recess this  is a big one  students must remain socially distant  whether in the building  or outside and teachers must watch to  ensure they remain  six feet apart the food service  department will also  be implementing a safety plan to give  out lunches safely  and then while some parents are looking  forward to this some teachers say  there is confusion over cohorts the  guide also has sample schedules it talks  about the airflow on the school buses  and demonstrates the classroom layout  i'm very confident in their health and  safety measures they're going to take  for the children  as well as their transition timeline if  we're going to be going back in the  classroom we have to  really you know be able to have a  manageable workload that is the biggest  thing  the head of the cdc says we should not  wait until all teachers are vaccinated  there was a study last week from the cdc  doctors that showed schools  that reopened in the fall did not  contribute to the spread of coveit 19  in any meaningful way and we have a link  to ccsd's full 235 page guide on our  website  at 8newsnow.com reporting bianca holman  8 news no